{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent low bias: model forecasts are systematically below realized prices, especially during sustained uptrends. Apply an upward level shift (larger in the first ~20 forecast days).",
    "Trend underreaction / lag: when the last 1–2 weeks show strong momentum, the model increases too slowly versus reality. Add a momentum-based uplift proportional to recent slope/returns.",
    "Horizon shape error: early horizon (≈days 1–20) is most underpredicted; late horizon (≈days 25–30) often turns too bearish/flat versus outcomes. Use a horizon-dependent bias correction that decays but stays positive through day 30.",
    "Over-mean-reversion after spikes: following sharp rises, the model reverts down too quickly while the market stays elevated. Reduce mean-reversion strength when recent volatility is high and trend is positive.",
    "Downturn timing: when the true series eventually rolls over, the model tends to call the pullback too early and too deep. Delay and dampen negative adjustments unless confirmed by multiple consecutive down days."
  ]
}
